WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.099
Question eleven. Highlight: convert decimal “forty-three” to “hexadecimal”.

00:00:06.099 --> 00:00:10.735
Useful: divide by sixteen; remainder eleven is written B.

00:00:10.735 --> 00:00:15.208
Useless: sensor story — does not change the conversion.

00:00:15.208 --> 00:00:21.145
Option A. Two five hex: two times sixteen plus five = thirty-seven — cut.

00:00:21.145 --> 00:00:27.000
Option B. Two B hex: two times sixteen plus eleven = forty-three — keep.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:32.856
Option C. Two D hex: two times sixteen plus thirteen = forty-five — cut.

00:00:32.856 --> 00:00:38.711
Option D. Two F hex: two times sixteen plus fifteen = forty-seven — cut.

00:00:38.711 --> 00:00:44.323
Forty-three equals two times sixteen plus eleven — hexadecimal two B.

00:00:44.323 --> 00:00:47.088
Therefore the correct answer is B.
